Unhandled errors in Express default to leaking stack traces to the client. This exposes file paths, dependency names, and internal logic.

**Fix — add a global error handler as the last middleware:**
```js
// Must be defined AFTER all routes
app.use((err, req, res, next) => {
  // Log internally with full detail
  console.error({
    message: err.message,
    stack: err.stack,
    path: req.path,
    method: req.method,
    timestamp: new Date().toISOString(),
  });

  // Return nothing useful to the client
  const statusCode = err.status ?? 500;
  res.status(statusCode).json({
    error: statusCode < 500 ? err.message : 'An internal error occurred',
  });
});
```

