  auditLog('users.list', { userId: req.user.id, ip: req.ip });
  // ...
});
```

---

### 🟡 MEDIUM — `app.listen` in the Module Body

**Reliability / Testability**

Calling `app.listen()` in the same file that does `module.exports = app` causes the server to start a port listener when the module is `require()`d in tests, leading to port conflicts, hard-to-test code, and unclear separation of concerns.

**Recommendation:**

```js
// app.js — only configure the app
module.exports = app;

// server.js — entry point, only starts the listener
const app = require('./app');
const PORT = process.env.PORT || 3000;
app.listen(PORT, () => console.log(`Server running on port ${PORT}`));
```

---

## Summary Table

| Severity | Issue | OWASP | Fix |
|---|---|---|---|
| 🔴 Critical | Credentials file in project directory | A02 | Gitignore + secrets manager + rotate keys |
| 🔴 Critical | No authentication on any endpoint | A01 | JWT/session middleware on protected routes |
| 🔴 Critical | No security headers | A05 | `helmet()` |
| 🟠 High | No input validation | A03 | `zod`/`joi` schema validation |
| 🟠 High | No rate limiting | A04 | `express-rate-limit` |
| 🟠 High | PII exposure in `/users` | A02 | Response DTOs + access scoping |
